{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 11bc3eafacc5b920d4763d47c59aa3d6d91c6d90, tree 757bd66e912c761aeb63d5fa8989eba804477f7b. This clarity rewrite retains the two findings filed in draft-4 review e3c73ac9. It improves readability but explicitly changes no rule, and neither finding has been resolved at this head. All findings are below.\n\nF1 — P1 — Bind derivation to the prospective effective commit’s identity and time (sections 5.2, 5.4 and 6.1). The prepare holds derived effects/sends, and the later commit must carry identical bytes. Ordinary derivation uses head.seq+1 as self; opening effects and self refs therefore point at the prepare’s sequence, while native fold requires an opened item’s ID to equal the effective entry.seq. With head H, an ordinary prepared opening names H+1 and the effective commit is H+2. Existing fold rejects that opening. Relaxing the fold would break item/fact identity. Define the prospective effective-entry sequence/self context before deriving, including openings by handlers, self refs and sends carrying the new item. The fence makes the future sequence knowable; do not rewrite sealed prepared bytes afterward.\n\nTime is still contradictory without a declared context rule. Step 5 freezes all judgments at the pre-prepare clock and never judges again, while 6.1 defines late against the effective commit’s clock. Source time0 plus within10 is fresh when prepared at5 and late when committed at20 after a lost resolution reply or eviction. Frozen branch selection plus a normal later commit time cannot satisfy both statements. Specify a frozen effective judgment time, a separate retained judgment-time field, or another precise choice, and its clamping/notAfter/deadline/late/replay rules. A write fence does not stop physical time.\n\nRequired controls: an admitted sequenced open act and opening handler with self refs and a send carrying the new item, verified through native item/fact reads and replay; and lost-resolution/eviction across a late boundary and derived deadline. Record the prospective identity/time inputs in the S3–S5 handoff. The prior choice that commit is the only effective fact remains sound; its derivation context is what is missing. The native rules supporting this counterexample are judge.ts/handlers.ts (self=head.seq+1), effects.ts (opening and self ref derivation), fold.ts:105 (opening ID=entry.seq), and entryOf’s clock/sequence assignment in judge.ts. This is design analysis, not an executed unimplemented runtime.\n\nF2 — P2 — Fix section 5.9’s refused-input and expiry costs. It still says one order entry for a refused input. A normal judgment refusal after allocation writes the allocation and then its hole: two order entries, zero member entries. A refusal before allocation writes zero. Expiry is an allocation’s outcome rather than an unconditional additional outcome entry; a retry is another attempt. Separate and hand-count these paths so the cost table matches 5.3/5.4.\n\n1. Fidelity. Draft 5 is a clearer statement of draft 4: the terms now have one place, and the effective-fact, reservation/settlement, cut/genesis/leave, post-close, failure-model, source-order and amended late-object choices remain. It carries the older fixes from review47cd6158. It does not answer the subsequent identity/time and cost findings in e3c73ac9, which this review carries forward without adding a new finding.\n\n2. Correctness. Approval remains withheld on F1 and F2. The one-effective-fact consumer list and explicit commit/abandon and allocation-outcome reservations are not reopened. Runtime, native transport, low-capacity and replay/clone witnesses remain future obligations. Clearer prose does not supply their results.\n\n3. Evidence and scope. I read all 957 lines of the primary first, then the unchanged scopes paragraph and the authored delta. Independent scratch materialization checked every Git blob of the 2,118 regular leaves: only the note and docs/scopes.md differ from authored base feccbbcf, and all other 2,116 source/test leaves remain unchanged. Relative draft4, only this note changes. Whitespace passes. Base tree b5a0a28f1b0809bf5b090689761ff5557f3c5998 and candidate tree 757bd66e912c761aeb63d5fa8989eba804477f7b qualify for the documents-only no-repeat rule in docs/testing.md; no unchanged suite or gate was run. Evidence: /private/tmp/checker-order-draft5-uw2q0z3o/validation.json.\n\nThe branch is still based on feccbbcf, so an eventual landing must preserve newer Main, including M2a. This review accepts no S-slice runtime, package-note implementation, provider effect, publication or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3d7bc0e567520340b73526758cd45644d13d9ef9","binding":"assigned","head":"11bc3eafacc5b920d4763d47c59aa3d6d91c6d90","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8202ac201e30c1cbf7555dcc83937a984a10a548\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3e4a926151f6bdb386dade53b343c35eef2496dd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6ab80d6312dd64833ace9802cb257072c2dfa1d0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}